question:
You review a Bicep file containing the following resource declaration:

resource stg 'Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts@2023-01-01' = {
  name: 'appstg${uniqueString(resourceGroup().id)}'
  location: 'eastus'
  sku: {
    name: 'Standard_LRS'
  }
  kind: 'StorageV2'
}

What is the primary function of the uniqueString(resourceGroup().id) function in this declaration?

You examine an ARM JSON template that contains the following parameter definition:

"adminPassword": {
  "type": "securestring",
    "metadata": {
    "description": "Administrator password for the VM."
  }
}

Which statement accurately describes how Azure Resource Manager handles this parameter?

You inspect a Bicep file that includes an existing resource reference:

resource vnet 'Microsoft.Network/virtualNetworks@2023-05-01' existing = {
  name: 'prod-vnet'
}

How does Bicep treat this resource during deployment?

An ARM template defines the following section:

"resources": [
  {
    "type": "Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines",
    "name": "[parameters('vmName')]",
    "dependsOn": [
      "[resourceId('Microsoft.Network/networkInterfaces', parameters('nicName'))]"
    ]
  }
]

What is the impact of the 'dependsOn' element in this ARM template?

You are reviewing a Bicep module declaration:

module vnetModule './vnet.bicep' = {
  name: 'vnetDeploy'
  params: {
    vnetAddressPrefix: '10.0.0.0/16'
  }
}

What does this construct achieve?

You analyze a Bicep resource that includes a loop:

resource storageAccounts 'Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts@2023-01-01' = [for name in accountNames: {
  name: name
  location: 'eastus'
  sku: { name: 'Standard_LRS' }
  kind: 'StorageV2'
}]

Assuming 'accountNames' is an array of 3 strings, what will Bicep create?

An ARM template includes an outputs section:

"outputs": {
  "fqdn": {
    "type": "string",
    "value": "[reference(resourceId('Microsoft.Network/publicIPAddresses', parameters('publicIPName'))).dnsSettings.fqdn]"
  }
}

What is the purpose of this outputs section?

You see the following Bicep conditional resource definition:

resource appGateway 'Microsoft.Network/applicationGateways@2023-05-01' = if (deployAppGateway) {
  name: 'prod-agw'
  location: location
}

What happens when the parameter 'deployAppGateway' is evaluated as false during deployment?

